<style is:global>
  .hero-stage {
    /* Stable aspect ratio so percentage-based layout scales together on
       resize. floating-man-new-fade.png (1024 × 870) at 92 % stage_W;
       shifted with `-right-[24.56%]`. Right-edge fade is baked into the
       asset; not hard-cropped. No vertical clip — full image height is
       preserved. */
    aspect-ratio: 1024 / 768;
    line-height: 0;
    width: 100%;
    overflow: visible;
    /* Extend the paint region on the sides so the man's fade can spill
       past the right edge AND the leftward shift below doesn't get
       clipped on the left. Top/bottom are cropped by 5 px each. */
    clip-path: inset(20px -35% 35px -10%);
    /* The 35 px bottom clip above hides the lowest 35 px of the man
       image but the element still occupies that space in the DOM,
       which leaves a visible bg-stone-50 strip between the man and
       the next section. Pull the stage up by the same amount so the
       visible bottom of the man sits flush against the section
       boundary, with no leftover background sliver. */
    margin-bottom: -35px;
    /* Nudge the whole hero (sensors, dashboard, floating-man, fade)
       left as one block so the sensor column tucks in just under the
       Logo + Products area of the nav. Percentage is of `.hero-stage`'s
       own width, so the shift scales with the viewport — everything
       inside the stage moves together, no internal layout changes. */
    --hero-shift-x: -8.91%;
    transform: translateX(calc(var(--hero-shift-x) - 35px));
  }

  /* Banner backdrop. Fills the hero-stage and is masked to be visible
     only behind the dashboard tablet:
       •   0 % –  22 %  : transparent  (stone-50; fade starts left of the
         dashed-line midpoint at ~32 %)
       •  22 % –  40 %  : soft fade-in (gentler ramp over 18 % width)
       •  53 % – 100 %  : full peak (atrium runs to the right edge;
         the fade tail extends past the stage so the right edge stays
         fully visible — the man's own arm fade in the PNG keeps the
         body crisp) */
  .hero-backdrop {
    --backdrop-lines-mid: 22%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: right bottom;
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(
      to right,
      transparent 0,
      transparent var(--backdrop-lines-mid),
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1) calc(var(--backdrop-lines-mid) + 3%),
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.24) calc(var(--backdrop-lines-mid) + 6%),
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4) calc(var(--backdrop-lines-mid) + 9%),
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.58) calc(var(--backdrop-lines-mid) + 12%),
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.78) calc(var(--backdrop-lines-mid) + 15%),
      black calc(var(--backdrop-lines-mid) + 18%),
      black 100%,
      transparent 112%
    );
    mask-image: linear-gradient(
      to right,
      transparent 0,
      transparent var(--backdrop-lines-mid),
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1) calc(var(--backdrop-lines-mid) + 3%),
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.24) calc(var(--backdrop-lines-mid) + 6%),
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4) calc(var(--backdrop-lines-mid) + 9%),
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.58) calc(var(--backdrop-lines-mid) + 12%),
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.78) calc(var(--backdrop-lines-mid) + 15%),
      black calc(var(--backdrop-lines-mid) + 18%),
      black 100%,
      transparent 112%
    );
  }

  /* man.png — soft 3 % gradient on the very right edge so the silhouette
     dissolves smoothly instead of ending in a hard line. */
  .hero-overlay {
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(
      to right,
      black 0%,
      black 97%,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.95) 97.7%,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6) 98.4%,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35) 99.1%,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15) 99.7%,
      transparent 100%
    );
    mask-image: linear-gradient(
      to right,
      black 0%,
      black 97%,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.95) 97.7%,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6) 98.4%,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35) 99.1%,
      rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15) 99.7%,
      transparent 100%
    );
  }

  /* Geometry for the dashboard-inside-tablet alignment.
     ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Only the dashboard scales — the sensor column on the left stays
     at its full natural size. The scale lives INSIDE the SVG (on the
     `.dashboard-group` transform attribute) so it does not affect the
     sensors, and the sensors are simply moved as a unit by changing
     their `transform="translate(...)"` to sit under the SENSORS label.

     Hero-stage:  aspect 1024/768 = 1.3333 (W:H, 4:3)
       → stage_H = 75.000 % of stage_W.
     Floating-man-new-fade PNG: 1024×870, aspect 1.1768. Bottom-anchored at
       width = 92 % of stage_W with `-right-[32.54%]` so the tablet
       cutout stays aligned; right leeway fades via mask (not cropped).
       • Image left  =  40.540 % of stage_W
       • Image right = 132.540 % of stage_W   (extends past stage, faded)
       • Image top   ≈ −4.25 % of stage_H  (full height, not cropped)
       • Image bot   = 100.000 %
     Tablet screen cutout — measured by finding rows that have BOTH a
     left bezel (opaque at x≈101-112) AND a right bezel (opaque at
     x≈530-545), so transparent regions outside the tablet (above,
     below, left of bezel) are excluded:
       x = 10.84 – 51.76 % of image-W  (width 40.92 %)
       y = 26.44 – 70.80 % of image-H  (height 44.36 %)
     With the image at 33.42 % left (-right-[25.42%]), 92 % wide,
     104.21 % of stage_H tall, bottom-anchored at 100 %:
       horiz: 43.39 – 81.04 % of stage_W
       vert:  23.34 – 69.57 % of stage_H
     Outer-left bezel at image x ≈ 101 → stage 42.49 % → wrapper x≈511,
     ~30 px left of the "S" in SOLUTION on a 1150 px-wide stage.

     SVG (viewBox 1024×600) renders preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet";
     SVG fills stage_W, height = 78.13 % of stage_H, vertically centred
     (top margin 10.94 % of stage_H). Mapping:
       SVG-x = stage_x_% · 10.24
       SVG-y = (stage_y_% − 10.94) / 78.13 · 600

     Tablet cutout in wrapper coords (+76 for the wrapper's
     `<g transform="translate(-76 0)">`):
